{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27890225","formula":"C₁₅H₂₁NO","hill":"C15H21NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Cis-(−)-metazocine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Metazocine is an opioid analgesic related to pentazocine. While metazocine has significant analgesic effects, mediated through a mixed agonist–antagonist action at the mu opioid receptor, its clinical use is limited by dysphoric and hallucinogenic effects which are most likely caused by activity at kappa opioid receptors (where it is a high-efficacy agonist) and/or sigma receptors. Metazocine is in Schedule II of the Controlled Substances Act 1970 of the United States as a Narcotic with ACSCN 9240 with a 19 gram aggregate manufacturing quota as of 2014."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":443404,"mass":231.33,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H]1[C@H]2CC3=C([C@@]1(CCN2C)C)C=C(C=C3)O","inchikey":"YGSVZRIZCHZUHB-COLVAYQJSA-N","iupac":"(1R,9R,13R)-1,10,13-trimethyl-10-azatricyclo[7.3.1.02,7]trideca-2(7),3,5-trien-4-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"443404","atoms":38,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.303,"y":0.213,"z":-0.717,"el":"O"},{"x":2.622,"y":-0.643,"z":-0.634,"el":"N"},{"x":0.496,"y":1.33,"z":-0.189,"el":"C"},{"x":1.618,"y":1.033,"z":0.853,"el":"C"},{"x":2.033,"y":-0.448,"z":0.708,"el":"C"},{"x":1.1,"y":1.065,"z":-1.597,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.697,"y":0.38,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":0.845,"y":-1.368,"z":1.064,"el":"C"},{"x":1.716,"y":-0.333,"z":-1.74,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.505,"y":-0.9,"z":0.571,"el":"C"},{"x":0.095,"y":2.819,"z":-0.108,"el":"C"},{"x":1.252,"y":1.396,"z":2.302,"el":"C"},{"x":3.247,"y":-1.95,"z":-0.809,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.988,"y":0.726,"z":-0.437,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.598,"y":-1.77,"z":0.722,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.063,"y":-0.152,"z":-0.287,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.